      <p class="text-sky-900">
        An RCIC (Regulated Canadian Immigration Consultant) is an immigration consultant licensed by the College of Immigration and Citizenship Consultants (CICC), the federal regulator set up under the College of Immigration and Citizenship Consultants Act. Before you pay anyone, search their name on the CICC public register at register.college-ic.ca and confirm "Active" status and "Yes" under Entitled to Practise. Only CICC licensees, members of a Canadian law society and Quebec notaries can charge for immigration advice, and you never need a representative to apply.
